MAGE - the image being edited (your character, the photo to\nrestyle, the scene...).\n\nTwo-image mode (group 2 enabled): THIS slot is always the SCENE\n(image 1). The person always goes in group 2 (image 2).\nInputs around 1MP work best. Two-person images: stay at/below ~1.5MP."], "inputs": [], "flags": {}, "type": "Note", "mode": 0, "bgcolor": "#653", "size": [520, 190], "pos": [495.18310546875, 622.661865234375], "id": 122, "properties": {"ue_properties": {"widget_ue_connectable": {}, "input_ue_unconnectable": {}, "version": "7.8"}, "widget_ue_connectable": {}, "Node name for S&R": "Note"}, "order": 3}, {"outputs": [], "color": "#432", "widgets_values": ["OPTIONAL second reference - the PERSON for insert-into-scene edits\n('place this person at the table').\n\nThis group ships DISABLED (purple = bypassed) - the workflow is a\nplain single-image editor until you need it.\nEnable: right-click this group's title bar -> toggle Bypass off.\nOrder rule: scene = image 1 (group 1), person = image 2 (here)."], "inputs": [], "flags": {}, "type": "Note", "mode": 0, "bgcolor": "#653", "size": [520, 210], "pos": [495.18310546875, 1422.6612548828125], "id": 123, "properties": {"ue_properties": {"widget_ue_connectable": {}, "input_ue_unconnectable": {}, "version": "7.8"}, "widget_ue_connectable": {}, "Node name for S&R": "Note"}, "order": 4}, {"outputs": [], "color": "#432", "widgets_values": ["Write the edit in plain English:\n  'Relight the scene with warm golden hour sunlight.'\n  'Place this person at the cafe table, holding a coffee.'\n  'Change her outfit to a red raincoat.'\n\nUnique face coming out generic? Append:\n  'Preserve the exact facial identity - distinguishing features: ...'\nand describe what makes the face distinctive.\n\ngrounding_px: how large the model 'sees' the input while reading your\ninstruction. 384-768 is the trained range. Getting doubled/split\ncompositions? LOWER it. The collapsed node below is the negative -\nonly used at CFG > 1; keep its prom